architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/reviews/round-01-review.md:33:Good improvement: it removes obsolete API surface and forces explicit action-group ownership. However, as written it leaves `DependencyService.rebuildDependencyMaps()` / `getActionDependencies()` as residual compatibility surface even though the scope check shows those methods are already deprecated no-ops and active tests still rely on them. That weakens the claimed “single dependency boundary.”
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/reviews/round-01-review.md:41:Partially. It aggressively deletes `ProcessTree.addAction()`, `World.addAction()`, `ProcessTree.getActionsDependingOnElement()`, and obsolete implicit-group tests. But it stops short of clearly deleting the deprecated `DependencyService` compatibility shims the scope check already identifies as dead residue.
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/reviews/round-01-review.md:65:Mostly, but it is missing one explicit focused check for the dependency-shim deletion decision. If Wave 005 deletes `rebuildDependencyMaps()` and `getActionDependencies()`, validation must name focused dependency-service or deletion-cascade tests that prove no caller still depends on rebuild semantics.
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/reviews/round-01-review.md:79:- `DependencyService.rebuildDependencyMaps()` is explicitly deprecated and no-op in current code (`frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts`).
