architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/proposals/proposal-direct.md:92:Wave 005 intentionally does **not** extract broad process-history use-cases from `ActionsPanel.vue` or remove its direct imports of process-tree operation classes. That work belongs with Wave 006's UI command-construction/use-case boundary so it can be solved consistently across `ActionsPanel.vue`, `SvgCanvas.vue`, toolbar/tool handlers, and related command construction surfaces. Wave 005 may touch `ActionsPanel.vue` only for narrow boundary-honesty cleanup needed by the deleted APIs: misleading dependency comments, debug logging, or compile fixes. Any new `frontend/src/application/processTree/*UseCases.ts` module would be a scope deviation requiring a mini-cycle.
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/proposals/proposal-direct.md:96:User-visible behavior should remain equivalent for construction history, undo/redo, subprocess stack navigation, action-group display, deletion cascade, persistence replay, and ActionsPanel interactions. Developer-facing behavior changes intentionally: code can no longer call `ProcessTree.addAction()` or `World.addAction()` to create an implicit group, code can no longer ask `ProcessTree` for dependency dependents, and code/tests can no longer call `DependencyService.rebuildDependencyMaps()` or `DependencyService.getActionDependencies()` as no-op compatibility hooks. Callers must use explicit action-group creation and the real `DependencyService` registration/query API.
