architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/scope-check.md:34:`ProcessTree.addAction(action, groupName?)` still exists and is explicitly marked deprecated because it implicitly creates action groups and has historically broken undo logic (`frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:143`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:144`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:145`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:148`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:150`). `World.addAction(action: any, groupName?: string): any` remains as a loose proxy to that deprecated path (`frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:904`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:907`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:908`).
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/scope-check.md:36:Active tests still encode the obsolete implicit-group path: `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts` calls `tree.addAction(...)` in multiple tests for single action insertion, group-name creation, chronological ordering, recursive traversal, removing an action, and output collection (`frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:36`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:47`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:59`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:97`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:115`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:140`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:161`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:172`). Deletion/factory tests also bypass command-tracked group creation by calling `world.getProcessTree().addAction(...)` directly (`frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:55`, `frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:86`, `frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:87`, `frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:88`; `frontend/tests/unit/commands/removeElementOps.spec.ts:43`). These tests are obsolete under the wave target and should be rewritten or deleted.
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/scope-check.md:40:`ProcessTree.getActionsDependingOnElement(elementId)` still exists, is documented as deprecated in favor of `DependencyService.getDependents(elementId)`, logs a warning, and returns an empty array (`frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:401`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:403`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:404`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:406`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:407`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:411`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts:412`). Its unit tests are already skipped because dependencies are no longer stored in actions (`frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:179`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:180`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:184`, `frontend/tests/unit/processTree.spec.ts:188`). This is dead compatibility surface and should be deleted, not wrapped.
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/scope-check.md:44:`DependencyService` is now a domain-local stateful container (`frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:42`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:49`). It owns node registration/unregistration, dependency queries, dependent traversal, and invalidation traces (`frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:67`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:90`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:150`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:180`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:278`). However, it also keeps deprecated no-op process-era methods such as `rebuildDependencyMaps()` and `getActionDependencies(_actionId)` (`frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:130`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:131`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:306`, `frontend/src/domain/world/DependencyService.ts:317`). Tests still call `world.getDependencyService().rebuildDependencyMaps()` in deletion scenarios (`frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:93`, `frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:132`, `frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:168`, `frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:264`, `frontend/tests/unit/commands/factories/DeletionSequenceFactory.spec.ts:312`; `frontend/tests/unit/commands/removeElementOps.spec.ts:132`). These no-op dependency shims are in scope for Proposal Restructure and may be included in Proposal Direct if the reviewer agrees they are part of the same ownership cleanup.
architecture-audit/cycle-005-process-tree-dependency-ownership/scope-check.md:68:The strongest direct implementation target is to delete `ProcessTree.addAction()`, delete `World.addAction()`, delete `ProcessTree.getActionsDependingOnElement()`, rewrite/delete tests that encode implicit group creation, and tighten process-tree tests around `addActionGroup()` + `addActionToGroup()` and operation-mediated insertion. The restructure alternative should evaluate removing remaining no-op dependency shims and introducing a small process-history application boundary that ActionsPanel can call, but the implementation should avoid pulling all Wave 006 UI command-controller work into Wave 005 unless review explicitly chooses that higher-level fix.
